{
 "id": "20260926-060449-interaction-replay-wrap-onepass",
 "axis": "interaction",
 "hypothesis": "First transcript frame of a resumed session pays quadratic time in the TUI wrap of unbroken tokens longer than the wrap width: markdown.rs wrap_spans_into re-measured str_width(&rest) and cloned the remaining tail per emitted row, O(token_len^2/width) for the 10MiB stock fixture's ~4.3MB single-word pad row (~22s of a ~21s-to-ready cold open). Upstream TUI laziness (bc412c5f) does NOT absorb it; the fix removes the re-measure and the tail clone, tracking remaining width arithmetically with a one-true-measure backstop at the tentative exit for non-additive grapheme-cluster splits.",
 "approach": "crates/pa-tui/src/markdown.rs wrap_spans_into only: remaining width measured once, decremented per row, rest sliced in place (zero tail clones); correctness backstop re-measures once at the tentative exit when a row split lands inside a multi-char grapheme cluster. Tests: embedded verbatim legacy algorithm as the output oracle (full Vec<Line> equality incl. span styles + render-vs-count rows), adversarial ZWJ-family repro across widths 1-40, mixed Unicode/escape/OSC-8/multispan corpora, bounded differential corpora, 1MiB monoword stress (content round-trip + ceil row count, no wall-clock assert). Measured on VM bmxeyxz112wjq2g5wn7o82k0: pure-base control at d5cd4b132, then same-head B,C,C,B pairs at three successive upstream bases (sha-asserted binary swaps, per-trial canonical fixture prehash, pre/mid/post calibration), per-process RSS probes incl. a t0+20s double-sample, and a styled first-frame byte-parity probe on the real stock attach corpus.",
 "parity_notes": "Complexity fix, never a layout change: embedded legacy-oracle differential tests prove byte- and style-identical wrap output across corpora incl. adversarial grapheme cases; end-to-end styled first-frame dump on the real 10MiB stock attach capture is byte-identical base-vs-cand (fnv1a digest 59a4ef8715652ad8, sha256 11e9782847c90415666202d09e3f13a8fa88793f9ae429cc943252ce504d4f96, 24 lines / 4284 styled bytes, both sides); all pinned stock trials emit identical pty_bytes (5555) on both sides; sentinel/echo/erase validation identical. Claim scope: long-unbroken-token worst case ONLY - never generic large-session resume (50x1MiB capped toolResult blobs render 13.7ms; real 2717-msg session 4.7ms; daemon create+attach ~0.7s).",
